 startTransition(async () => {\"},{\"charStart\":2343,\"charEnd\":2386,\"text\":\"      const error = await updateName(name);\"},{\"charStart\":2460,\"charEnd\":2484,\"text\":\"      redirect(\\\"/path\\\");\"},{\"charStart\":2525,\"charEnd\":2603,\"text\":\"      <input value={name} onChange={(event) => setName(event.target.value)} />\"},{\"charStart\":2605,\"charEnd\":2663,\"text\":\"      <button onClick={handleSubmit} disabled={isPending}>\"},{\"charStart\":2665,\"charEnd\":2679,\"text\":\"        Update\"},{\"charStart\":2752,\"charEnd\":2996,\"text\":\"The async transition will immediately set the isPending state to true, make the async request(s), and switch isPending to false after any transitions. This allows you to keep the current UI responsive and interactive while the data is changing.\"},{\"charStart\":2998,\"charEnd\":3077,\"text\":\"Note\\nBy convention, functions that use async transitions are called “Actions”. \"},{\"charStart\":3079,\"charEnd\":3132,\"text\":\"Actions automatically manage submitting data for you:\"},{\"charStart\":3134,\"charEnd\":3801,\"text\":\"Pending state: Actions provide a pending state that starts at the beginning of a request and automatically resets when the final state update is committed.\\nOptimistic updates: Actions support the new useOptimistic hook so you can show users instant feedback while the requests are submitting.\\nError handling: Actions provide error handling so you can display Error Boundaries when a request fails, and revert optimistic updates to their original value automatically.\\nForms: <form> elements now support passing functions to the action and formAction props. Passing functions to the action props use Actions by default and reset the form automatically after submission.\"},{\"charStart\":3803,\"charEnd\":4105,\"text\":\"Building on top of Actions, React 19 introduces useOptimistic to manage optimistic updates, and a new hook React.useActionState to handle common cases for Actions. In react-dom we’re adding <form> Actions to manage forms automatically and useFormStatus to support the common cases for Actions in forms.\"},{\"charStart\":4107,\"charEnd\":4159,\"text\":\"In React 19, the above example can be simplified to:\"},{\"charStart\":4161,\"charEnd\":4203,\"text\":\"// Using <form> Actions and useActionState\"},{\"charStart\":4205,\"charEnd\":4245,\"text\":\"function ChangeName({ name, setName }) {\"},{\"charStart\":4247,\"charEnd\":4305,\"text\":\"  const [error, submitAction, isPending] = useActionState(\"},{\"charStart\":4307,\"charEnd\":4347,\"text\":\"    async (previousState, formData) => {\"},{\"charStart\":4349,\"charEnd\":4408,\"text\":\"      const error = await updateName(formData.get(\\\"name\\\"));\"},{\"charStart\":4462,\"charEnd\":4486,\"text\":\"      redirect(\\\"/path\\\");\"},{\"charStart\":4547,\"charEnd\":4579,\"text\":\"    <form action={submitAction}>\"},{\"charStart\":4581,\"charEnd\":4620,\"text\":\"      <input type=\\\"text\\\" name=\\\"name\\\" />\"},{\"charStart\":4622,\"charEnd\":4686,\"text\":\"      <button type=\\\"submit\\\" disabled={isPending}>Update</button>\"},{\"charStart\":4721,\"charEnd\":4725,\"text\":\"    \"}],\"sourcePath\":\"C:\\\\Temp\\\\weftmate-fact1-a005538c-526b-4fdb-8ed3-53c99dfd017e\\\\profile\\\\conversations\\\\6f251f14e18ce83a71420ceb53ec71361bc053a2062a1dffa2503a346043a73a\\\\session-028bf3ad-3995-4bc2-92b4-45bb76407c22\\\\.weftmate-web-sources\\\\capture-2f5065b4-2c03-4b02-96fc-f9db45b7aee7.txt\"}"
