er export condition for use in frameworks that support the Full-stack React Architecture.\\n\\n[characters 11798-11849]\\nNote\\nHow do I build support for Server Components? \\n\\n[characters 11851-12096]\\nWhile React Server Components in React 19 are stable and will not break between minor versions, the underlying APIs used to implement a React Server Components bundler or framework do not follow semver and may break between minors in React 19.x.\\n\\n[characters 12098-12371]\\nTo support React Server Components as a bundler or framework, we recommend pinning to a specific React version, or using the Canary release. We will continue working with bundlers and frameworks to stabilize the APIs used to implement React Server Components in the future.\\n\\n[characters 12373-12424]\\nFor more, see the docs for React Server Components.\\n\\n[characters 12443-12529]\\nServer Actions allow Client Components to call async functions executed on the server.\\n\\n[characters 12531-12752]\\nWhen a Server Action is defined with the \\\"use server\\\" directive, your framework will automatically create a reference to the server function, and pass that reference to the Client Component. When that function is called o\",\"truncated\":true,\"query\":\"forwardRef ref prop class component cleanup function ref\",\"excerpts\":[{\"charStart\":292,\"charEnd\":367,\"text\":\"The date for this post has been updated to reflect the stable release date.\"},{\"charStart\":1188,\"charEnd\":1213,\"text\":\"function UpdateName({}) {\"},{\"charStart\":1835,\"charEnd\":1988,\"text\":\"In React 19, we’re adding support for using async functions in transitions to handle pending states, errors, forms, and optimistic updates automatically.\"},{\"charStart\":2104,\"charEnd\":2129,\"text\":\"function UpdateName({}) {\"},{\"charStart\":2998,\"charEnd\":3077,\"text\":\"Note\\nBy convention, functions that use async transitions are called “Actions”. \"},{\"charStart\":3134,\"charEnd\":3801,\"text\":\"Pendin